WEBVTT

00:30.210 --> 00:31.460
Reine.

02:18.690 --> 02:21.060
Good morning, Reine.

02:21.690 --> 02:22.340
Hmm?

02:24.970 --> 02:28.750
Was I actually just—

02:29.090 --> 02:30.890
Yes, you fell asleep.

02:31.420 --> 02:34.000
Though only for about five minutes.

02:36.890 --> 02:37.860
Reine?

02:45.560 --> 02:47.520
Reine's laughing.

02:47.850 --> 02:52.770
This is the first time I've heard 
Analyst Murasame laugh.

02:53.290 --> 02:54.740
I see.

02:54.740 --> 02:56.070
I did, huh?

02:57.620 --> 03:00.230
Well then, I've lost.

03:03.840 --> 03:06.430
U-Um, what's gotten into you?

03:07.150 --> 03:08.620
You have my thanks.

03:09.050 --> 03:12.040
It's been a long time 
since I fell into a pleasant sleep.

03:13.060 --> 03:16.920
Your shoulder must have been quite comfortable.

03:18.230 --> 03:18.920
<i>Shido!</i>

03:19.340 --> 03:22.550
There's a fluctuation in Reine's 
affection and mental state!

03:22.900 --> 03:23.680
Do it now!

03:25.380 --> 03:26.430
Reine.

03:26.740 --> 03:29.680
Hmm? Why are you looking serious?

03:30.060 --> 03:31.140
Earlier...

03:31.780 --> 03:34.540
you mentioned having someone you loved,

03:37.390 --> 03:39.070
but could I be that man?

03:41.200 --> 03:44.440
I know I'll never be a replacement for them.

03:44.440 --> 03:51.330
But would you let me love you in 
my own way that's different from them?

03:55.370 --> 03:56.380
Reine.

04:03.570 --> 04:06.020
Shin, I...

04:14.740 --> 04:15.850
We did it!

04:23.170 --> 04:23.880
Commander!

04:23.880 --> 04:25.110
These numbers are abnormal!

04:25.110 --> 04:26.120
Huh?

04:36.170 --> 04:38.380
Her spirit power isn't flowing into me?!

04:44.820 --> 04:48.890
I see. You've seen the future, huh?

04:50.260 --> 04:52.230
What are you so surprised for?

04:52.860 --> 04:56.010
It's possible to share memories 
once a pass is formed.

04:56.620 --> 04:59.400
It's not your first time 
experiencing it, right?

05:00.030 --> 05:02.420
Now I've solved the mystery behind today.

05:02.900 --> 05:07.030
No, I think I might have vaguely sensed it,

05:07.030 --> 05:09.270
but I imagine I didn't want to understand it.

05:10.370 --> 05:14.780
Because I was very happy 
when you invited me on a date.

05:15.990 --> 05:17.830
I really did have fun.

05:18.770 --> 05:23.220
So much so that I was able to forget 
my harsh past for a short time.

05:24.130 --> 05:27.610
Though all dreams must come to an end.

05:28.170 --> 05:29.250
Isn't that right,

05:30.930 --> 05:31.830
Shido?

05:35.100 --> 05:36.960
<i>Shido! It's DEM!</i>

05:36.960 --> 05:37.690
Huh?!

05:46.590 --> 05:49.510
It would seem history's been rewritten.

05:52.260 --> 05:55.620
Would you return to Fraxinus with me, Reine?

05:56.280 --> 05:57.880
After we defeat DEM,

05:57.880 --> 06:01.300
you could live together with me 
and all the other Spirits.

06:01.730 --> 06:03.860
I'm sure every day would be fun.

06:04.370 --> 06:07.710
Yes, that's a very attractive offer.

06:08.900 --> 06:13.910
I'm sure I would've taken it up without 
a second thought if I hadn't met Shin.

06:14.380 --> 06:15.350
Then—!

06:15.350 --> 06:16.720
But I can't.

06:17.350 --> 06:19.740
Because I did meet Shin.

06:20.670 --> 06:24.970
It's a genuine fact that 
I love all the Spirits too,

06:24.970 --> 06:30.410
but I'm willing to throw away everything 
if it means reuniting with Shin.

06:43.750 --> 06:44.880
Kurumi?!

06:44.880 --> 06:46.130
Why?!

06:47.430 --> 06:50.900
"Why?" is quite the greeting.

06:50.900 --> 06:54.890
Especially when I came running to your aid.

06:54.890 --> 06:56.530
Kurumi, huh?

06:56.530 --> 06:58.320
I'm glad you came.

06:58.320 --> 07:00.640
Having you here makes things quick.

07:00.980 --> 07:06.590
My, my, you're as arrogant 
and intolerable as ever,

07:06.590 --> 07:08.650
Spirit of Origin.

07:09.420 --> 07:13.540
I can't believe I let you completely fool me.

07:13.540 --> 07:18.160
I never even imagined 
my bitter enemy would be so close by.

07:18.580 --> 07:20.140
Either way,

07:20.140 --> 07:25.170
this means the remaining two Sephirah 
possessed by you and Westcott

07:25.170 --> 07:27.310
have been gathered here.

07:28.100 --> 07:30.920
That's enough to awaken Shin.

07:31.240 --> 07:35.090
Well now, I wonder 
if it will go that easily for you?

07:52.980 --> 07:55.220
I'm taking them back, Kurumi.

07:55.710 --> 07:59.540
Both the Sephirah inside you, 
and my other half.

07:59.540 --> 08:01.910
Hah! I refuse to let you!

08:08.500 --> 08:10.760
Come to me, Kurumi.

08:17.690 --> 08:18.740
Kurumi!

08:23.620 --> 08:26.430
I've been waiting for this moment!

08:29.740 --> 08:31.010
Zaphkiel!

08:37.340 --> 08:38.280
Kurumi?

09:13.740 --> 09:14.860
Mio.

09:15.340 --> 09:17.930
It's been a long time since you've
seen me in this form.

09:18.640 --> 09:25.620
No, you've already met me in this form 
in a future I don't know of, haven't you?

09:25.620 --> 09:27.620
That's a bit complicated.

09:33.690 --> 09:36.130
You don't have Kurumi's Sephirah?

09:36.790 --> 09:39.810
That girl must have done something.

09:40.250 --> 09:43.640
Leave it to my dear best friend.

09:52.540 --> 09:53.780
Shin?

09:59.590 --> 10:00.950
Are these?!

10:01.370 --> 10:02.950
DEM warships approaching!

10:03.290 --> 10:05.450
They'll be entering firing range at any moment!

10:05.450 --> 10:07.530
Shido, we're retrieving you.

10:07.530 --> 10:09.580
Then we're taking a moment to regroup.

10:09.980 --> 10:12.590
Shin, what's the matter?

10:12.590 --> 10:13.590
Shin?

10:18.100 --> 10:20.860
He was taken back by Fraxinus?

10:22.070 --> 10:24.970
I suppose that might be 
the safest place for him right now.

10:27.730 --> 10:30.570
It wouldn't be very nice if those crude wizards

10:30.980 --> 10:34.550
and automatons destroyed this scenery.

10:35.230 --> 10:36.740
Ein Sof Ohr!

10:42.170 --> 10:42.780
Shido!

10:42.780 --> 10:43.490
-Shido!

10:42.780 --> 10:43.490
-Darling!

10:42.780 --> 10:43.490
-Boy!

10:42.780 --> 10:43.490
-Master!

10:45.050 --> 10:47.000
Tohka, everyone...

10:47.370 --> 10:48.840
Are you all right?

10:48.840 --> 10:50.750
Did Mio do anything to you?

10:51.020 --> 10:56.380
No, though I was a little confused from 
Mio's memories flooding into me all at once.

10:56.380 --> 10:57.810
I'm fine now.

10:57.810 --> 10:59.450
Commander, that's...

11:05.020 --> 11:08.020
So that's Ein Sof Ohr?

11:08.370 --> 11:11.020
The Spirit of Origin's Angel...

11:11.020 --> 11:14.520
I had heard about it, 
but I didn't realize it was that powerful.

11:14.810 --> 11:18.650
Let's fall back while DEM 
is keeping Mio occupied.

11:18.650 --> 11:19.610
We can't!

11:19.890 --> 11:20.720
Hmm?

11:20.720 --> 11:21.770
We can't!

11:21.770 --> 11:23.370
I can't run away yet!

11:23.930 --> 11:25.380
What are you saying?!

11:25.380 --> 11:26.840
Our operation has failed.

11:26.840 --> 11:29.870
We need to withdraw and think of our next move.

11:31.690 --> 11:35.000
<i>Someone is seeking communication with us.</i>

11:35.000 --> 11:36.880
<i>What shall I do, Kotori?</i>

11:38.410 --> 11:40.630
All right, put them through.

11:42.880 --> 11:44.510
Shido! Look!

11:45.770 --> 11:47.850
Huh? The school?

11:48.410 --> 11:49.730
What's going on?

11:51.500 --> 11:54.480
Captain, Mike, and Milly?

11:56.280 --> 11:58.010
Yuzuru, that's...!

11:58.010 --> 12:01.110
Astonishment. That's our classroom.

12:01.540 --> 12:03.610
What is this?

12:14.140 --> 12:15.750
Is it a terrorist?!

12:15.750 --> 12:17.250
What's going on?!

12:22.230 --> 12:25.760
<i>It's exactly as you see, members of Ratatoskr.</i>

12:26.140 --> 12:27.760
Westcott!

12:28.810 --> 12:31.500
<i>It's good to do things 
like this now and then, isn't it?</i>

12:31.500 --> 12:33.610
<i>Now that Deus has manifested,</i>

12:33.610 --> 12:37.150
<i>I'd like to finish up our business 
as quickly as possible.</i>

12:37.520 --> 12:39.650
Are you threatening us?!

12:39.650 --> 12:42.780
There's no deal to be had here though.

12:43.180 --> 12:47.900
If we hand the Sephirah over to you, 
you'll just overwrite the entire world.

12:47.900 --> 12:49.790
That would defeat the entire point.

12:50.350 --> 12:56.370
Then I'll simply murder those girls 
as brutally as possible.

12:57.380 --> 13:03.300
If even one Spirit inverts, 
then that's enough for me.

13:17.560 --> 13:19.080
What's going on?!

13:19.080 --> 13:22.220
Design-wise, these aren't 
heroes of justice, are they?

13:22.220 --> 13:24.900
They're more like minions of evil, if anything.

13:24.900 --> 13:26.310
That's so lame.

13:27.390 --> 13:28.980
Help!

13:28.980 --> 13:35.530
I wanted to bury my face in a woman's 
thighs at least once before I died!

13:35.530 --> 13:38.530
E-Everyone, please hurry up and run!

13:38.530 --> 13:40.880
We're already surrounded, though!

13:49.140 --> 13:50.050
Huh?

13:55.860 --> 13:58.220
Are you okay, Ai, Mai, Mii?

13:58.220 --> 14:00.150
Also, Tonomachi and Tama.

14:01.530 --> 14:02.810
Tohka?!

14:02.810 --> 14:03.960
Yatogami?!

14:03.960 --> 14:05.030
That's so lame!

14:05.400 --> 14:08.030
Everyone, stick together in one spot!

14:30.410 --> 14:32.220
O-Origami?!

14:44.120 --> 14:45.110
Good!

14:45.610 --> 14:48.850
Hmm, it looks like everyone made it in time.

14:48.850 --> 14:51.310
Though I was worried 
about long-distance transit.

14:51.620 --> 14:57.250
Oh, god, will we be able to cover 
all this up, even with Ratatoskr's power?

14:57.250 --> 14:59.120
My stomach is already upset at the thought.

14:59.490 --> 15:00.370
Hmm...

15:00.690 --> 15:04.380
Still, we weathered that, Isaac Westcott!

15:04.690 --> 15:07.330
<i>That truly was a brilliant showing.</i>

15:07.330 --> 15:11.260
<i>Though one always keeps 
their trump card in reserve.</i>

15:11.690 --> 15:13.090
What was that?

15:16.130 --> 15:19.210
<i>A DEM warship has rammed Fraxinus.</i>

15:19.210 --> 15:23.420
<i>It appears to be synchronizing 
its territory and docking with ours.</i>

15:25.200 --> 15:27.900
Goetia! Ellen Mathers?!

15:32.620 --> 15:36.180
It's delusional to think 
you're safe inside your warship.

15:36.180 --> 15:39.060
At least it is when facing me!

15:49.630 --> 15:52.320
One always keeps their trump card in reserve.

15:52.320 --> 15:55.930
That certainly is a nice phrase, 
coming from a brutish president.

15:56.340 --> 15:57.430
Mana!

16:03.600 --> 16:05.270
Shido, that's reckless!

16:07.760 --> 16:09.400
Mana!

16:16.340 --> 16:19.090
My, my, the siblings all together.

16:19.090 --> 16:21.170
Would you let me join in too?

16:23.830 --> 16:24.920
Nibeelcole!

16:31.070 --> 16:32.670
Westcott!

16:34.740 --> 16:36.930
What's happening to the DEM warships?

16:37.180 --> 16:39.310
They're under attack from Ein Sof Ohr!

16:39.310 --> 16:42.060
Several ships have suffered major damage 
and their formation is in disarray!

16:42.380 --> 16:47.970
He's targeting Shido while the warships 
are drawing Mio Takamiya's attention.

16:48.610 --> 16:51.500
I can't believe he's willing 
to use entire warships as bait...

16:51.500 --> 16:53.320
That's a bold move.

16:53.320 --> 16:55.700
This is no time to be impressed.

16:56.060 --> 16:58.450
I'm leaving the bridge to you, Kannazuki.

16:58.720 --> 16:59.380
Yes, ma'am!

17:03.210 --> 17:04.190
Brother!

17:08.310 --> 17:11.370
Here's some nostalgic faces all together.

17:11.370 --> 17:14.590
It feels like I've gone back into the past.

17:14.590 --> 17:16.900
Yeah, that's true.

17:16.900 --> 17:20.260
Neither you nor Ellen have moved on since then.

17:20.260 --> 17:25.100
Though normally one would show 
at least some growth after all this time.

17:25.500 --> 17:29.850
Honestly, I would love to 
reminisce about old times,

17:29.850 --> 17:32.460
but unfortunately I'm short on time.

17:32.890 --> 17:37.490
I'll be finishing this 
before your Spirits return.

17:41.100 --> 17:41.940
Tsk!

17:41.940 --> 17:45.260
If you're talking about 
siblings being together,

17:45.260 --> 17:47.510
then aren't you forgetting one of us?

17:49.400 --> 17:50.510
Kotori!

17:50.910 --> 17:52.640
There's no other choice.

17:52.640 --> 17:56.810
Mukuro needs to maintain the portals 
so everyone can return,

17:56.810 --> 17:59.710
and Nia doesn't have the power left to fight.

18:00.140 --> 18:02.640
That means I'm the only one left.

18:02.970 --> 18:04.300
But still...

18:04.300 --> 18:05.680
Don't worry.

18:05.680 --> 18:10.140
I can wield my power for a bit before getting 
overwhelmed by my destructive impulse.

18:10.140 --> 18:13.780
It would be a bad joke if I couldn't do 
anything during an emergency like this.

18:14.210 --> 18:15.260
Kotori...

18:15.260 --> 18:16.530
Kotori...

18:19.770 --> 18:21.160
Sandalphon!

18:23.080 --> 18:24.160
Wolftail!

18:26.010 --> 18:26.910
Camael!

18:33.210 --> 18:36.170
Here we come, Isaac Westcott!

18:36.170 --> 18:40.100
We'll show you the combined might 
of us three siblings!

18:40.100 --> 18:41.550
Right, Kotori?

18:41.880 --> 18:44.680
Are we really three siblings?

18:44.970 --> 18:47.530
This isn't the time for nitpicking details.

18:53.420 --> 18:54.810
Amusing.

18:54.810 --> 18:58.700
Try and fight your fate, humans.

19:10.290 --> 19:13.670
We'll soon arrive at the battlefield, Elliot.

19:16.270 --> 19:17.810
Deus...

19:17.810 --> 19:19.180
Mio, huh?

19:20.120 --> 19:24.150
It's the Spirit we all summoned 
thirty years ago.

19:24.980 --> 19:27.450
In order to get revenge on mankind.

19:28.220 --> 19:33.140
Good grief, I fell for quite the evil woman.

19:36.900 --> 19:43.320
Though if Deus is going to fight the other 
Spirits, then I can't leave her alone.

19:44.230 --> 19:45.720
Which should we protect?

19:45.720 --> 19:48.380
That's obvious. Both.

19:48.870 --> 19:50.190
Both?

19:50.730 --> 19:53.020
Do you think that's even possible?

19:53.630 --> 19:56.090
It would be impossible on my own.

19:56.090 --> 19:58.840
But that boy,

19:59.580 --> 20:05.660
Shido Itsuka should be 
thinking the same thing I am.

20:07.510 --> 20:09.790
So you're going then, Elliot?

20:10.290 --> 20:11.510
Yeah.

20:11.510 --> 20:14.480
Karen, I'm counting on you to prepare Wodan.

20:17.340 --> 20:22.110
Do you find it hard to believe 
that the man who betrayed his allies

20:22.580 --> 20:28.260
in order to protect a Spirit 
would risk his life to fulfill that duty?

20:29.070 --> 20:33.610
I've followed you this far 
precisely because you're like that.

20:39.710 --> 20:42.220
Please, Karen.

20:43.510 --> 20:46.130
<i>Sir Woodman, we're awaiting your orders.</i>

20:47.710 --> 20:48.510
<i>This is...</i>

20:48.860 --> 20:50.180
<i>This response is...</i>

20:57.770 --> 20:58.900
Brother!

20:57.770 --> 20:58.900
Shido!

21:00.400 --> 21:01.360
Shido!

21:01.360 --> 21:02.150
Brother!

21:12.300 --> 21:14.540
Now, this is the end.

21:14.850 --> 21:18.290
Dammit! It can't end here!

21:45.090 --> 21:50.410
Now then, it's finally time 
to repay that favor,

21:51.910 --> 21:54.950
<b>Episode 10</b>

21:51.910 --> 21:54.950
<b>A Battlefield That Shouldn't Be Possible</b>

21:52.280 --> 21:53.730
Shido.

23:24.960 --> 23:39.980
Episode 11: "A Fleeting Paradise"

23:26.080 --> 23:29.020
Everyone has a summer they'll never forget.

23:29.470 --> 23:33.210
Next time is Episode 11: A Fleeting Paradise.

23:33.720 --> 23:35.600
"If only I could regain that happiness."

23:36.060 --> 23:39.130
Is it really a sin to wish for that?
